# Algorithms for Resource Allocation of Substance Abuse Prevention Funds Based on the Estimated Need: A Case Study on State of Florida--Part 1.

**Authors:** Kim, Sehwan, Wurster, Leslie, Williams, Charles, Hepler, Nancy

## Abstract
The first of three articles that develop a framework for county-based prevention-resource-allocation algorithms based on the aggravated need for substance-abuse-prevention services estimated at the county level. Algorithm development is based on (1) statewide student drug survey, and (2) a set of social indicators routinely published by agencies in Florida. (Author/MKA)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ574935

